From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix ghost beacon on Radio.Enable=0

wld_autoCommitMgr_destroy/init in the disable path of
reconfigureNeighLinkAPs cancelled pending FSM commits even when no
sibling was actually notified. On all-radio-disable or last-link-disable
this wiped the disabling radio's own Stop hostapd commit, leaving
hostapd running (ghost beacon).

Guard destroy/init with a notifiedSibling flag so it only fires
when at least one enabled sibling was actually told to rebuild.

Signed-off-by: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
index ef3b83b..166ea9c 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
@@ -233,6 +233,7 @@
      * a group, isLinkUsable=false but isLinkEnabled=true; using isLinkEnabled
      * prevents false entry into the disable path for the re-join case. */
     if((pLink != NULL) && !wld_mld_isLinkEnabled(pLink)) {
+        bool notifiedSibling = false;
         wld_for_eachNeighMldLink_safe(pNgLink, pLink) {
             if(pNgLink == pLink) {
                 continue;
@@ -247,15 +248,22 @@
                 wld_mld_saveLinkConfigured(pNgLink, false);
                 setBitLongArray(pNgAP->fsm.FSM_BitActionArray, FSM_BW, GEN_FSM_MOD_MLD);
                 wld_autoCommitMgr_notifyVapEdit(pNgAP);
+                notifiedSibling = true;
             }
         }
         /* Serialize sibling MOD_MLD commits AFTER the disabling radio FSM commit
          * (Stop hostapd) completes. At 10+ MLD groups, sibling wpaCtrl sockets
          * reconnect faster than Stop hostapd, causing setMldParams to rebuild
          * with the 2.4GHz link still present. destroy/init resets the autoCommit
-         * timer so siblings execute after the current commit cycle finishes. */
-        wld_autoCommitMgr_destroy(pSSID->RADIO_PARENT);
-        wld_autoCommitMgr_init(pSSID->RADIO_PARENT);
+         * timer so siblings execute after the current commit cycle finishes.
+         * Only apply when siblings were actually notified: when all links are
+         * disabled simultaneously (Radio.*.Enable=0) or the last link in a group
+         * is disabled, no siblings are notified and destroy/init would cancel the
+         * disabling radio's own Stop hostapd commit, causing a ghost beacon. */
+        if(notifiedSibling) {
+            wld_autoCommitMgr_destroy(pSSID->RADIO_PARENT);
+            wld_autoCommitMgr_init(pSSID->RADIO_PARENT);
+        }
         return SWL_RC_OK;
     }
     wld_for_eachNeighMldLink_safe(pNgLink, pLink) {
--
